{
    "background_story": "Preston was a brilliant scientist who spent most of his life studying the intricacies of the universe. His groundbreaking research on dark matter was met with skepticism by his peers, who deemed his theories inconsiderable and unproven. Undeterred, Preston continued to work tirelessly in his small laboratory, pouring over data and conducting experiments. Years went by, and his work remained largely unnoticed. However, when a team of renowned astrophysicists stumbled upon an anomaly in the cosmic microwave background radiation, they were forced to revisit Preston's research. It turned out that his supposedly inconsiderable theories were, in fact, the key to understanding the phenomenon. Overnight, Preston's work was catapulted to the forefront of the scientific community, and he was hailed as a visionary. His story serves as a reminder that even the most seemingly inconsiderable ideas can hold immense significance.",
